{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:68b8535b89e20a9c","name":"Swamp Gas","source":{"id":"source:reference-68b8535b89e20a9c","title":"Swamp Gas","revision":26553,"timestamp":"2025-03-26T06:32:58Z","sha256":"2baecd8f0d3d992ee5269ecb9e4827c83cfedcafb8cb8f3f73e2e0632c766547","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=26553","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Swamp%20Gas&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-68b8535b89e20a9c","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Unknown Regions Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Unknown_Regions_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["A near-transparent cloud of gas is exuded by decomposing matter in a swamp."]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Virtually undetectable to the naked eye, Swamp Gas can be troublesome when it drifts into an occupied area, especially around creatures that are capable of making a fire. Combatants who detect the presence of the gas during combat often try to use it to their advantage, such as by firing a blaster bolt through the gas when it is near an opponent or setting off a grenade near the gas to boost the destructive power of the explosion. Clever creatures might capture Swamp Gas in a breakable container and use it as a grenade.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Swamp Gas Statistics (CL 4)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Keywords:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Area"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Area"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Atmosphere"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Atmosphere"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fire"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fire","referenceId":"reference:c141faa80e43a119"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Natural"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Natural"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Trigger:"]}," A spark or energy source comes into contact wi